    "id": "miq_165",
    "question": "In a group of 15 high school students, 7 study Latin, 8 study French, and 3 study neither Latin nor French. How many students study both Latin and French?",
    "options": [
      "3",
      "4",
      "15",
      "None"
    ],
    "correct_answer": "3",
    "explanation": "📝Question: In group of 15 high school students, 7 study Latin, 8 study French and 3 study neither latin nor French. How many students study both Latin and French.<br/>❏ Solution:<br/>There are a group of 15<br/>3 have not studied either.<br/>∴ The number of student who either studied Latin or French = 15 - 3 = 12<br/>❏ Here, <br/>The number of student studied Latin = n(L) = 7<br/>The number of student studied French = n(F) = 8<br/>❏ Let,<br/>The number of student studied both Latin and French = n(L &cap; F)<br/>❏ Now,<br/>n(L &cup; F) = n(L) + n(F) - n(L &cap; F)<br/>⇒ n(L &cap; F) = n(L) + n(F) - n(L &cup; F)<br/>= 7 + 8 - 12<br/>= 15 - 12 <br/>= 3<br/>❏ ∴ 3 students of these studied both Latin and French",
