    "correct_answer": "a decrease of 1%",
    "explanation": "📝 <b>Question:</b> If the price of an item is increased by 10% and then decreased by 10% , the net effect on the price of the item is -<br/>❐ <b>Solution:</b><br/>❐ Let,<br/>❐ The price of an item is 100 Tk.<br/>❐ If the price increased by 10%,<br/>❐ So, the new price will be after increased = 100 + {100 × (10/100)} Tk.<br/> = 100 + 10 Tk.<br/> = 110 Tk.<br/>❐ Then the new price decreased by 10%,<br/>❐ So, the new price will be after decreased = 110 - {110 × (10/100)} Tk.<br/> = 110 - 11 Tk.<br/> = 99 Tk. <br/>  ∴  The net effect on the price of the item is = (100 - 99) Tk. decreased<br/> = 1 Tk. decreased",
